      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3423315513,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Thanks for catching that. We initially [pulled in the speex resampling code directly](3687d39304). It was later split of into a separate library dependency. A quick search turned up libsamplerate if we want to use an alternative external library, but it doesn't look like there's a Fedora MinGW package for that. We could switch back to built-in code with something like clownresampler. We could also just declare that Fedora's MinGW packages don't have everything we need and stop building on that platform.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
